{"id": "EUVD-2015-9431", "enisaUuid": "6767c70d-1e4c-35a5-aa7e-ee9a2a5208c3", "description": "Aspose PDF Exporter plugin for WordPress before 2.0 contains a path traversal vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to download files through the unsanitized 'file' parameter passed to readfile(). Attackers can send GET requests to aspose_pdf_exporter_download.php with traversal sequences like ../../../wp-config.php to retrieve WordPress database credentials. Exploitation evidence was first observed by the Shadowserver Foundation on 2023-10-19.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T20:31:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T20:31:25", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://packetstorm.news/files/id/131161/", "https://wpscan.com/vulnerability/51dd0b6b-ba90-47e2-ad80-56b3e122bfd4", "https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/changeset/1127209/aspose-pdf-exporter", "https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/vulnerabilities/wordpress/aspose-pdf-file-download.yaml", "https://wordpress.org/plugins/aspose-pdf-exporter/", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/aspose-pdf-exporter-wordpress-plugin-2.0-path-traversal-via-aspose-pdf-exporter-download-php"], "aliases": ["CVE-2015-20125", "GHSA-p7cr-5mhm-8gc2"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.41, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "dd6c1eba-ba7a-3834-a47c-540773a1a9b0", "product": {"name": "Aspose PDF Exporter", "vendor": {"name": "Aspose"}}, "product_version": "1.0 <2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d3f84534-996f-3e64-98ae-4051952c56d1", "vendor": {"name": "Aspose"}}], "isExploited": false}